# The project video, as a cue sheet.
#
# Every frame is the real plugin rendering through the real FFGL sequence -- this
# is the generator being *operated*, not a mock-up. Render with:
#
#   ./build/idtest --sequence /tmp/id-frames --script tools/video.cues \
#                  --size 1920x1080 --seconds 52 --fps 30 --text "IDLER"
#
# Syntax: `T Name=V` sets at a time, `T1..T2 Name=V1..V2` ramps between the two
# (eased, because a parameter that starts and stops abruptly reads as a cut).
#
# Every value here is the 0..1 the host sees, not the physical quantity -- see
# Controls.h for why there is no other kind. Option parameters are the exception
# and carry the element index: Saver 0..10, Shading 0 Flat / 1 Lit / 2 Wireframe,
# Colour Mode 0 Classic / 1 Tint / 2 Spread / 3 Cycle.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING HERE SETS `Preset`, AND IT MUST NOT.
#
# Cues are applied in file order on EVERY frame, not once when their time comes.
# A `Preset` cue would therefore re-apply for the whole rest of the piece -- and
# because editing any preset-covered parameter flips the dropdown back to Custom,
# a `Preset` cue and a ramp of anything it covers fight each other once per
# frame: the ramp sets the value and clears the preset, the preset cue sees the
# change and copies its whole row back over the top. The picture flickers between
# two sets of parameters at 30Hz and the cue sheet looks correct.
#
# So each saver's scene is set out in full below. It is more lines and it is the
# only version that renders what it says.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The order of the piece: the flat ones first, in the order they appeared on the
# machine, then the OpenGL ones -- ending on 3D Pipes and 3D Text, because the
# pipes are what everybody actually remembers and the text is the one that can
# carry a sign-off.

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 0s: Mystify
# The one people picture when you say "screensaver". Opens mid-motion rather
# than from nothing: Phase is offset so the trails are already there on frame 1.
0 Saver=0
0 Density=0.55
0 Complexity=0.35
0 Size=0.5
0 Length=0.45
0 Line Width=0.25
0 Variation=0.5
0 Shading=0
0 Speed=0.5
0 Phase=0.12
0 Seed=0.0
0 Fog=0.0
0 Colour Mode=0
0 Opacity=1.0
0 Background Alpha=1.0

# The trail lengthens as the shot settles, which is the control worth showing
# first because it is the one that makes Mystify look like Mystify.
1.5..5.0 Length=0.45..0.8

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 5s: Beziers
# Density at 0.3 is a single curve, and a single Bezier through five bouncing
# points spends a lot of its life nearly straight -- the first cut caught it flat
# and the beat was an empty frame with a line in it. Two curves and a long trail.
5 Saver=1
5 Density=0.55
5 Complexity=0.45
5 Length=0.85
5 Line Width=0.28
5 Phase=0.05

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 9s: Curves and Colors
9 Saver=2
9 Density=0.25
9 Complexity=0.45
9 Size=0.6
9 Length=0.7
9 Line Width=0.2
9 Hue Cycle=0.55
# The ratio drifting off a whole number is what makes the figure precess rather
# than close and repeat. Shown by moving it.
9.5..13.0 Complexity=0.45..0.62

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 13s: Flying Windows
13 Saver=3
13 Density=0.45
13 Complexity=0.5
13 Size=0.5
13 Variation=0.4
13 Line Width=0.3
13 Field of View=0.45
13 Hue Cycle=0.5

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 17s: Flying Through Space
# Opens as it shipped -- white dots, no streaks -- then the streak comes up,
# which is the thing the original could not do.
17 Saver=4
17 Density=0.55
17 Size=0.35
17 Length=0.02
17 Complexity=0.5
17 Variation=0.5
17 Colour Mode=0
19.0..22.0 Length=0.02..0.75
19.0..22.0 Density=0.55..0.85
19.0..22.0 Speed=0.5..0.68

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 22s: Scrolling Marquee
# Density is copies IN FLIGHT, and at 2 the repeats overlap: the first cut read
# "RIDLERIDLE" across the frame, which is the saver working exactly as specified
# and completely illegible. One copy for the video.
22 Saver=5
22 Speed=0.5
22 Density=0.0
22 Size=0.5
22 Length=0.35
22 Line Width=0.45
22 Variation=0.0
22 Complexity=0.5
22 Colour Mode=0
22 Phase=0.0

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 26s: 3D Maze
# The first of the OpenGL ones. Lit, fogged, and walking.
26 Saver=6
26 Density=0.4
26 Complexity=0.4
26 Size=0.5
26 Variation=0.5
26 Shading=1
26 Field of View=0.4
26 Camera Tilt=0.5
26 Fog=0.55
26 Colour Mode=0
26 Speed=0.5

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 31s: 3D Pipes
# The headliner, and the longest beat. Starts nearly empty and fills, which is
# the whole behaviour -- so Phase is pulled back to zero here and then run
# forward, rather than dropping in on a finished network.
31 Saver=7
31 Density=0.62
31 Complexity=0.45
31 Size=0.5
31 Length=0.6
31 Variation=0.5
31 Shading=1
31 Field of View=0.4
# Camera Distance 0.5 put the box a long way off and the pipes read as a scribble
# in the middle of a black frame. 0.22 fills it.
31 Camera Distance=0.22
31 Fog=0.3
31 Colour Mode=0
31 Phase=0.03
31 Speed=0.5
# Phase is the scrub: the network grows to wherever the slider is put, because
# the state at any time is a replay from the seed. This is the plugin's one real
# argument, so it gets the longest beat in the piece.
31.5..38.5 Phase=0.03..0.34

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 39s: 3D Flying Objects
39 Saver=8
39 Density=0.5
39 Complexity=0.5
39 Size=0.5
39 Length=0.5
39 Variation=0.6
39 Shading=1
39 Fog=0.2
39 Camera Distance=0.5
39 Phase=0.05

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 43s: 3D FlowerBox
# Ends on wireframe, which is the shading mode this one rewards most and a look
# nothing in 1998 could do.
43 Saver=9
43 Density=0.5
43 Complexity=0.55
43 Size=0.55
43 Length=0.5
43 Line Width=0.3
43 Shading=1
43 Fog=0.0
43 Camera Distance=0.4
43 Colour Mode=0
45.5 Shading=2
45.5 Line Width=0.4

# ------------------------------------------------------------ 47s: 3D Text
# The sign-off. Tinted rather than Classic, because the last shot should show the
# suite under one colour scheme -- which is the thing that makes any of it usable
# behind a band.
47 Saver=10
47 Density=0.25
47 Complexity=0.35
47 Size=0.55
47 Length=0.4
47 Line Width=0.42
47 Shading=1
47 Fog=0.0
47 Camera Distance=0.45
47 Camera Tilt=0.52
# 3D Text rotates a full turn, as it did -- so for a lot of its cycle the
# lettering is seen from BEHIND and reads mirrored. That is correct behaviour and
# a poor last shot: the first cut signed off on "R3LDI". Phase is chosen so the
# turn passes through front-on at about 50s and the piece ends facing the camera.
47 Phase=0.145
47 Colour Mode=1
47 Colour=0.55
47 Colour_Green=0.8
47 Colour_Blue=1.0
47 Speed=0.42
